	isbn = {978-0-7494-6379-3},
	shorttitle = {Pirate nation},
	abstract = {"In 2008, 95\% of all music downloads were illegally obtained. In the same year, digital album sales increased by 36\%. Pirate Nation is the story of modern-day digital piracy and how it affects business, society and culture. It traces the origins, methods and motivations of modern-day digital pirates. Roanoke-based "Piracy Happens" blogger, Darren Todd, covers topics such as copyright, creativity and piracy's potential role in business, and also explores the idea of using file-sharing and remixing as an asset instead of a liability. Looking critically at both sides of the piracy issue, Pirate Nation explains intellectual property, explores whether some degree of piracy is inevitable and discusses the limitations of current copyright law"-- Provided by publisher},
